  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary funds statement (p7). Business-type has no single printed revenue total: receipts total = Sales 350,213 + Bond proceeds 1,985,000 + Grant income 10,120 (bond proceeds printed among nonoperating revenues, also under general revenues on p3, so recorded as a receipt line); expense total 2,235,178 is the Statement of Activities business-type expenses (p2) = operating 115,052 + principal 1,994,765 + loan fees 65,065 + interest 60,296. Beginning governmental cash not printed (null); ending cash 1,646,927 and certificates of deposit 36,729 from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4); county treasurer cash 10,426 is a separate asset line (the Statement of Net Position p1 prints cash 1,068,813 + restricted 578,115 = 1,646,928 and county treasurer cash 10,425; same 1,694,082 total, 1-dollar rounding between statements). Fund balance roll-forward 1,424,905 + 912,183 - 596,858 - 46,148 = 1,694,082 reconciles; business-type -45,383 + 2,345,333 - 2,235,178 + 46,148 = 110,920 reconciles. Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) left null as in the later years (cash basis). General Fund detail from the department combining schedule (pp13-14); the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (p9) is not recorded to avoid double counting. Statement function split differs from the department schedule by 2 dollars (general government 315,045 vs 315,047; environment and leisure 59,848 vs 59,846), rounding in the report. Law enforcement 6,214 (General department) is public safety (p9 lists it under Public safety). Park 'Debt service' 4,134 = General Fund principal payments (p5). No business-type detail lines (as FY2023/FY2024: Water and Sewer have no schedules). Street Fund budget '-' recorded as 0. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
}
